## Finding

The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471/) says “one issue, one fix queued”.
Its own computed table disagrees. The shared parser and the booking-v3 input hint
are separate faults. A parser-only change does not correct the form's hint.

<IncidentReview />

## What the desk's components actually show

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Why the written dedupe rule is unsafe

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) and the
[triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe/) say to merge matching subjects and to merge when
unsure. The live component uses cause, not subject. The accepted decision dates
from June 2024 and the shared layout marks it stale. “Accepted” does not mean
recently verified.

For Alder Physio, the same subject through form and app maps to different causes.
Kettle Books app and email reports can have different subjects but the same cause.
Unknown tenants have no known cause: do not merge them merely because the subjects match.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Proposed desk action

Keep the two date faults in separate tickets. Investigate unresolved symptoms.
Use tenant, form, channel and reproduction evidence before merging a report.
If the cause is unknown, hold it for triage rather than forcing it into #4471.
Read [proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/) before adopting
this change. Decision 0001 is preserved, not silently rewritten or declared superseded.

Do not equate “known” or “queued” with fixed. Engineering's 5 October update
reports the parser fixed and the hint not fixed because booking-v3 was retired.
The two GitHub tickets close for different reasons. No production verification
was performed by this review. Counts cover the 4 October 2026 export; the later
engineering outcome is recorded separately above.

